  "details": "1. Start up Pico's Streaming assistant,\n\n2. Launch Steam VR, controllers still seen as Pico 4\n\n3. Start VRChat, controllers seem to jump out of my hands and into a weird spot, before being seen in game as Oculus Touch controllers. \n\nIt makes my pointer 30 degrees off of what it is in Steam overlay, along with making my hands several inches away from my irl hands, making is really jarring. Because it moved it also thinks the rotation pivot is in a different spot. \n\nIt works perfectly fine when I use the third party program Virtual Desktop, vrchat is able to recognize the Pico 4 controllers, but it doesn't work on Pico's own software, both going through steam.",
